# Patterns here match paths in the destination directory (~), not the source.
#
# This file replaces the ~100 line inverted .gitignore the old layout needed.
# That file had to start with `/*` and then re-admit every tracked path with a
# matching `!path` / `path/*` pair, because the repository's working tree was
# $HOME itself and so every unrelated file in $HOME was a candidate. chezmoi
# keeps its source tree separate, so the default is already "manage nothing",
# and only genuine exceptions belong here.

# Repository documentation, not a dotfile. It sits at the source root so it
# renders on GitHub; without this line chezmoi would deploy it to ~/README.md.
README.md

# .secrets is a separate, local-only repository that happens to live in $HOME.
# It must never be managed here and must never reach this public repo. chezmoi
# would not pick it up on its own, but a stray `chezmoi add ~/.secrets` would,
# and that mistake is unrecoverable once pushed.
.secrets

# Everything under .pixi except the global manifest: the environments are
# gigabytes of solved packages that `pixi global sync` rebuilds from
# .pixi/manifests/pixi-global.toml.
.pixi/envs
.pixi/bin

{{ if not (index .schemes (index .themes .theme).scheme).starshipDir -}}
# This colour scheme has no starship configs, so ~/.config/starship.toml is left
# unmanaged. Managing it would point the symlink at a directory
# .chezmoiexternal.toml never checked out, and starship would read a broken link
# on every prompt.
#
# Unmanaged means left exactly as it is, not removed. On a fresh machine the
# file is simply absent and starship uses its own defaults. On a machine
# switching away from Rosé Pine the old symlink stays, so the prompt keeps Rosé
# Pine's colours while everything else changes. That mismatch is the price of
# the missing port, and `theme` says which variants have one.
#
# Currently: {{ .theme }} has no starship port.
.config/starship.toml
{{ end -}}
